;
; DEED clause modules: shared rules, v1.0.0 (DRAFT)
; Prose and rationale: docs/estate-reconciliation/A7-contractiles-descriptiles-anchor.adoc
; sections 7.1 (the affirmation members) and 11 (M3: `common` is the first
; clause module, and every later one borrows from it).
;
; A LIBRARY OF RULES, not a profile. It defines no clause of its own. Each
; clause module (anchor.abnf now; the J14 heads, the descriptile and edict
; forms after it) borrows these rules instead of restating them, so a rule
; has one definition when the modules are compiled together, as the
; grammar-vs-gate differential compiles them. Rules it borrows (string,
; symbol, token-sep, DQUOTE, DIGIT, hex-lc) are deed.abnf's, unchanged.
; Requires RFC 7405 (%s"..." case-sensitive string literals).

; --- String lists -------------------------------------------------------

str-list        = "(" [token-sep] [string *(token-sep string)] [token-sep] ")"
str-list1       = "(" [token-sep] string *(token-sep string) [token-sep] ")"
                ; str-list1 is non-empty.

; --- The chora id -------------------------------------------------------

chora-uuid8     = %s"#uuid" DQUOTE 8hex-lc "-" 4hex-lc "-" "8" 3hex-lc "-"
                  lc-variant 3hex-lc "-" 12hex-lc DQUOTE
                ; deed.abnf's uuid narrowed to version 8: A1 rule V8 puts the
                ; profile C UUIDv8 in deeds; the UUIDv5 stays in the registry.
                ; Used for a parent (anchor.abnf) and for :beholding-chora.
lc-variant      = "8" / "9" / %x61 / %x62
                ; RFC 9562 variant 10, lowercase only. deed.abnf's uuid-variant
                ; writes "a" / "b", which ABNF matches case-insensitively; the
                ; code points keep this rule as strict as deed_lint.

; --- Dates --------------------------------------------------------------

date-string     = DQUOTE date DQUOTE
date            = 4DIGIT "-" date-month "-" date-day
date-month      = "0" %x31-39 / "1" %x30-32
date-day        = "0" %x31-39 / %x31-32 DIGIT / "3" %x30-31
                ; YYYY-MM-DD, month 01 to 12 and day 01 to 31. SEMANTIC
                ; (validator-enforced, not expressible in ABNF): a real
                ; calendar date, so "2026-02-31" and "2025-02-29" are refused.

; --- The affirmation members (A7 7.1, DESCRIPTILE-SPEC §affirmation) ---

affirm-member   = ( %s":affirmed"    token-sep date-string )
                / ( %s":affirmed-by" token-sep affirmer )
                / ( %s":expires"     token-sep date-string )
affirmer        = %s"owner" / %s"agent" / symbol
                ; A symbol, not a string: who or what last affirmed the facts.
                ; "owner" and "agent" are named; any other symbol is the name
                ; of the check that affirmed them.
                ; SEMANTIC: on every descriptile, each member exactly once by
                ; default; :expires is not before :affirmed. A repo setting may
                ; relax the requirement, and a relaxation is authorised and
                ; reported, never silent (A7 ruling J4).
